// Service of benefits and due/cessation dates (general layer):
// R. 514-1 (debtor body: CAF residence default + MSA/Etat/L. 212-1/arrete
// derogations), R. 552-1 (regime transfer: primitive regime serves +
// reimbursement claim), R. 552-2 (due-from dates: next-month rule + five
// exceptions), R. 552-3 (cessation dates + post-death maintien to the
// last day of the third month), R. 552-4 (maintien applicability,
// amount, ongoing conditions), L. 552-4 (schooling pieces: 2022-09-01
// text + 1985 predecessor with three pieces), L. 552-7 (deceased child
// counts; ASF advance kept), D. 552-7 (ARS 1-June decree companion),
// R. 553-2 (pacs partners treated as concubins).
//
// D. 552-6 (competent State authority for L. 552-4; arrete authorship):
// four rules - DASEN under rector delegation + alternative delegate
// ("ou son delegue", PC-R04-02) + two ministerial order authorships.
// R. 552-2 II 3 and R. 552-3 II 2 (AEEH renvois to R. 541-7) and the
// R. 552-4 / R. 541-1 amount exception are owned by fr.pf.aeeh:
// recorded, not duplicated.
//
// DEONTIC MAP:
// - R. 514-1 - competence allocation (institutional statuses); the
//   default is defeasible, each derogation a defeater + its own status.
// - R. 552-1 - primitive-regime service (status) + liberty to claim
//   reimbursement from the other regime.
// - R. 552-2/3/4, L. 552-4/7, D. 552-7, R. 553-2 - date and counting
//   rules: institutional statuses, no personal duties. L. 552-4
//   retroactivity turns on an organ judgment ("motifs independants de
//   sa volonte", section 47.3 channel).
//
// INPUT CONTRACTS (month mechanics, boundary B-PFCORE-DATES-MOIS
// narrowed, not removed). The caller states first-day-of-month anchors
// (conditions month, demande month, death month, cessation month);
// rules derive due/cessation dates by month steps under SERVICE_MOIS.
// Backward month steps (CMG preceding month, ASF 3-month floor) are
// caller-stated anchors, never computed: no backward policy exists.
// R. 552-3 IV endpoints use month_end_of of the +3-month step (E-0084,
// PC-R03-01): last day of the third following civil month from the
// exact death date; no policy roll is relied upon.
// The R. 552-2 I / R. 552-3 I general rules yield to the II derogations
// by benefit/trigger guards (PreParE single-child/option, CMG, AJPP,
// AEEH-by-renvoi, ASF evasion-only and judicial-after-recovery), so one
// case derives at most one due date per anchor set. Cross-benefit cases
// for one person stay out of scope: the date heads key on the person
// only (B-PFCORE-DUES-KEY-PERSONNE).

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.pf.core version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:pf-core";

